First Author: Shou
Title: Pre-Operative Machine Learning for Heart Transplant Patients Bridged with Temporary Mechanical Circulatory Support
Source number: 46  ￼

Very short summary: This UNOS-based study developed an interpretable XGBoost model to predict 1-year mortality after heart transplantation in patients bridged with temporary mechanical circulatory support (tMCS). Five key findings were: (1) 1,584 adult isolated heart-transplant recipients on tMCS were included; (2) observed 1-year mortality was 12.1%; (3) from 498 pre-transplant variables, 43 were selected for the final model; (4) the XGBoost model achieved an AUC of 0.71 (95% CI 0.62–0.78); and (5) the most important predictors included recipient functional status, age, pulmonary capillary wedge pressure, cardiac output, ECMO use, and serum creatinine. Tables 1 and S2 plus Figures 1–4 were used directly for this extraction.  ￼

