	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The authors “constructed a machine learning model using extreme gradient boosting (XGBoost) with a 70:30 train:test split.” They positioned the work against existing pre-operative risk scores such as IMPACT and CARRS, so Linear Risk Score is the best comparator label. SHAP was explicitly used for interpretation, and a grid search optimized hyperparameters. Forty-three predictors were “automatically selected for inclusion in the final XGBoost model based on predictive utility.”  ￼

